<Base title="About"><section class="page-title narrow"><h1>About me</h1><p class="lead">{profile.role}</p></section><article class="prose narrow"><p>{profile.intro}</p><p>At Huawei Edinburgh Research Center (2022–2026), I developed multipath model-transfer systems integrated with vLLM-Ascend, model pipelining, accelerator API remoting, GPU/NPU profiling and memory-management mechanisms. Earlier, at Ericsson Research (2018–2022), I developed distributed cloud/edge runtime and resource-allocation systems.</p><h2>Research interests</h2><ul class="bullet"><li>LLM serving, inference latency and model-weight restoration</li><li>GPU/NPU runtimes, memory management and topology-aware data movement</li><li>Distributed systems, cluster process orchestration and edge computing</li><li>Resource allocation and shared ML infrastructure</li></ul><h2>Education</h2><ul class="bullet"><li><strong>PhD, Computing Science</strong> — Umeå University, Sweden (2013–2018). <a href={thesis.url}>Doctoral thesis ↗</a></li><li><strong>MSc, Computer Science</strong> — Uppsala University (2010–2012)</li><li><strong>BEng, Information Technology</strong> — Panjab University (2006–2010)</li><li><strong>Micro-degree, Data Science</strong> — KTH & Ericsson (2020–2021)</li></ul><h2>Contact</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> · <a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></p></article></Base>
